A clean, presentation-first look: no axis ticks, no chart junk, bold centred
titles, and faint gridlines only where you ask for them. The base
\code{theme_ezrmodel()} strips gridlines entirely (best for bar charts that carry
their own data labels); the \verb{_x} / \verb{_y} / \verb{_xy} variants add back faint major
gridlines on the named axes. \code{transparent = TRUE} makes the backgrounds
transparent for slides. All the \verb{plot_*()} helpers apply one of these for you.
